# SFT execution status v0.102

2026-09-22. The read-only census result is complete and the final Source CI
metadata is now `success` (run `35635788165`, attempt 1). Spark CI also passed.
No remote action was started in this turn.

## Safe next design, not yet authorized for publication

The exact SDK census reached the existing 250,000-descendant-node cap. Raising
that cap or rerunning the cleanup would weaken the reviewed bound and would not
be safe. The cleanup also cannot proceed from a partial map because it needs a
complete, stable descriptor census before any mutation.

The minimal safe successor is a **sharded, read-only metadata census**:

1. Enumerate only the exact SDK root's immediate child entries by metadata.
2. Census each child subtree independently, retaining the existing per-shard
   limits: 250,000 nodes, depth 48, 32 MiB cumulative relative-name bytes,
   and 64 GiB allocated blocks.
3. Retain only aggregate shard counts, cumulative allocated bytes, and fixed
   `shard_budget_hit`/identity/tree codes—never names, paths, payloads or
   exceptions.
4. Stop on any shard bound or identity/mount anomaly. Do not delete, run the
   setup probe, acquire an image, raise limits, or launch qualification.

This design preserves the current caps and avoids the unsafe inference that a
single capped global map is complete. It has not been implemented, published,
or run. A fresh bounded approval is required before creating a remote workflow
or executing it. Existing attempt 1 remains consumed; prior evidence and all
source bindings remain unchanged.

`production_eligible=false` and Gate 5 incomplete remain unchanged.
